// For all other items this is just dateListed.
// Lifetime age — always from the original list date, ignoring relists. Used on
// the item page alongside the cycle age so the seller sees true holding time.

// was backfilled to dateListed). Only items created via Stock Quick Add and
// later transitioned to listed will have meaningful non-zero values.
// Patch A — Days in stock for a stock-state item. Uses today as the endpoint.

// Returns the average days-to-sell for an item, accounting for return+relist cycles.
// For a simple sale: days from dateListed to dateSold.
// For a resold item: average of (sale1 days) and (sale2 days).
//   sale1 days = dateListed → first returnHistory loggedAt (proxy for original sale date)
//   sale2 days = _relistedAt → resaleDateSold
